# Trivy CVE exceptions — accepted risk only.
# FORMAT (one per line):  CVE-XXXX-YYYYY   # owner, reason, review-by YYYY-MM-DD
# Rules:
#   - Every entry REQUIRES a justification + review date.
#   - No entry may sit here past its review date without re-approval.
#   - Legacy (7.4/8.0) EOL CVEs are handled per-image in CI, not blanket-ignored.

# caddy only: go-jose/v3 in the upstream Caddy BINARY (not an apk package, so it
# cannot be patched in our layer). go-jose is used for ACME/JOSE; this platform
# terminates TLS upstream (Caddy on high ports behind an LB), so the path is not
# exercised. Awaiting an upstream Caddy rebuild with go-jose >= 3.0.5.
# owner: platform/security · review-by 2026-07-02
CVE-2026-34986

# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# UNFIXED Debian distro CRITICALs (no fix available upstream). The enforcing gate
# runs --ignore-unfixed so these do not gate, but they are recorded here as
# EXPLICIT, reviewed exceptions per the vulnerability-management policy. Each is
# an essential package that cannot be removed; reachability is minimal. Re-review
# every weekly scan and drop the entry the moment Debian ships a fix.
# Affects: php-cli/fpm/worker/frankenphp (+ nginx perl-base, unfixed variants).
# owner: platform/security · review-by 2026-07-20

# zlib1g — CVE-2023-45853 (MiniZip integer overflow). Debian: will_not_fix
#   (Debian does not build/ship the affected MiniZip). zlib is essential.
CVE-2023-45853
# perl-base — CVE-2026-42496 (fix_deferred) + CVE-2026-8376 (affected). perl-base
#   is Priority: required (dpkg depends on it); not invoked by PHP/nginx runtime.
CVE-2026-42496
CVE-2026-8376
# libsqlite3-0 — CVE-2025-7458 (affected, no fix). sqlite3/pdo_sqlite are bundled
#   in the official PHP image; apps use Postgres/Redis, not sqlite, in production.
CVE-2025-7458
# frankenphp base extras (no fix available):
#   libaom3 — CVE-2023-6879 (AV1 decoder); not used by the PHP app server path.
CVE-2023-6879
#   linux-libc-dev — CVE-2026-43185 (kernel headers; not executable code at runtime).
CVE-2026-43185
